M7 -- online per-seat opponent model: wiring into the v0.5 belief path

Dylan Nguyen, FishLab Research Project
Repository /Users/dylan/Documents/GitHub/fish optimization, base commit fe21e19
plus the lead session's working v0.5 (M1 + M2 + M8 as built in engine/src/v05.hpp).

NOT APPLIED.  engine/src/v05.hpp, factory.hpp and main.cpp are owned by the lead
session.  The mechanism itself lives entirely in the new, unprotected header
engine/src/v05_oppmodel.hpp, which is already in the tree; this patch is only the
wiring.  Design note: research/v05/results/M7-design.md.

Apply from the repository root:      git apply research/v05/patches/M7.patch
Check it first:                      git apply --check research/v05/patches/M7.patch

WHAT THE PATCH DOES

  engine/src/v05.hpp
    * includes v05_oppmodel.hpp;
    * adds nine V05Config knobs (m7, m7ask, m7decl, m7bias, m7cap, m7tcap,
      m7carry, m7sil, m7th), all individually ablatable;
    * gives V05Agent an m7::OppModel, fed from observe() AFTER Agent::observe so
      it always reads the post-event Knowledge (this is the ordering hazard the
      diagnosis found as defect H, avoided by construction);
    * carries the per-seat type posterior between deals ONLY while the agent
      keeps the same seat -- a seat change means the opponents at those indices
      are different players and the evidence is void.  Note that the arena's
      duplicate-block rotation flips seats every rotation, so `m7carry` can only
      engage under --rotations=1 or at a fixed table;
    * replaces the five Belief::sinkhornDisj / jointSequential* call sites with
      the tilted equivalents from the new header;
    * adds a SECOND posterior, belDecl, for the declaration path.  Gating the
      final pAlloc is not sufficient: feasibleAllocation and bestGuess CHOOSE the
      allocation from bel.marg, so a tilted marginal steers which allocation is
      proposed even when its confidence is scored untilted.  belDecl is the same
      fit at m7DeclWeight (default 0) and is built only when the two weights
      differ, so the extra Sinkhorn pass disappears when they do not.

  engine/src/factory.hpp
    * one appended block of option parsing.  No existing line is altered.

  engine/src/main.cpp
    * one new command, `fish m7check`: the divergence guard.  m7::fitTilted is a
      structural copy of Belief::sinkhornDisj with a generalised initialiser, and
      belief.hpp is frozen so that v0.4 stays byte-identical as the reference
      opponent.  m7check asserts the copy has not drifted, by requiring exact
      equality on every state visited with the model disabled.

VERIFIED WITH THE PATCH APPLIED TO A SANDBOX COPY OF THE TREE

  $ make                                       # clean build, no new warnings
  $ ./fish m7check --games=30 --seed=20260822 --a=v05:m7=0
    m7check: 1054 states, max |fitTilted(off) - sinkhornDisj| = 0   PASS
  $ ./fish m7check --games=20 --seed=777 --a=v05
    m7check:  698 states, max |fitTilted(off) - sinkhornDisj| = 0   PASS
  $ ./fish m7check --games=20 --seed=777 --a=v04
    m7check:  840 states, max |fitTilted(off) - sinkhornDisj| = 0   PASS

  Off-switch equivalence -- `v05:m7=0` on the patched binary reproduces the
  unpatched `v05` exactly (same statistics to every printed digit, two seeds):
    patched   v05:m7=0 vs v05:m7=0, 20 deals seed 31    ask acc 55.2529%  decl 4.5/g 97.7778%
    unpatched v05      vs v05     , 20 deals seed 31    ask acc 55.2529%  decl 4.5/g 97.7778%
    patched   v05:m7=0 vs v04     , 20 deals seed 90210 ask acc 54.4669% / 56.1667%
    unpatched v05      vs v04     , 20 deals seed 90210 ask acc 54.4669% / 56.1667%

  NOT VERIFIED: whether M7 helps.  See M7-design.md §5 -- 50-game sanity runs at
  two seeds disagree in SIGN on every cell, so nothing about strength is claimed
  and no parameter was chosen from them.


AMENDED BY THE VERIFICATION PASS (2026-08-22)

  The first version of this patch routed bestGuess, feasibleAllocation and the
  jointSequential* confidences through the declaration posterior but left
  evaluateSet's `cheap` product reading pTeamCard(), i.e. the TILTED belief.
  `cheap` gates the voluntary declaration through cfg.marginalGate and becomes
  v.pTeam in Fast mode, so M7 could still unlock a declaration at m7decl = 0 --
  the same class of leak the patch's own note describes, one call site short.
  The amended patch adds V05Agent::dPTeamCard() and uses it there; the ask path
  is untouched and still reads pTeamCard().  Off-switch equivalence and m7check
  are unchanged (re-verified below).  Against `withholder:k=6`, 25 deals seed
  515151, declaration accuracy moves 94.57% -> 95.34% -- the predicted direction,
  but 50 games, so no strength claim.

  Re-verified with the amended patch applied to a sandbox copy:
    $ make                                       # clean build, no new warnings
    $ ./fish m7check --games=30 --seed=20260822 --a=v05:m7=0   -> 1054 states, 0  PASS
    $ ./fish m7check --games=20 --seed=777 --a=v05             ->  700 states, 0  PASS
    patched v05:m7=0 vs v04, 20 deals seed 90210: ask acc 54.4669% / 56.1667%
    unpatched v05    vs v04, 20 deals seed 90210: ask acc 54.4669% / 56.1667%

